# indexOf looks at the kind of storage once, integers first. A list of at most sixteen elements is searched in place; a longer one goes, by a rare edge, to a search in the run time.
# CHECK-LABEL: name="find" role=Source
# CHECK: Int32 b@[[byte]] = Load8Z(b@[[list]], offset = 4, ControlDependent|Reads:JSCell_indexingTypeAndMisc)
# CHECK: Int32 b@[[kind]] = BitAnd(b@[[byte]], $14(b@{{*}}))
# CHECK: Int32 b@[[isIntegers]] = Equal(b@[[kind]], $4(b@{{*}}))
# CHECK: Branch(b@[[isIntegers]], Terminal)
# CHECK: Int64 b@[[storage]] = Load(b@[[list]], offset = 8, ControlDependent|Reads:JSObject_butterfly)
# CHECK-NEXT: Int32 b@[[length]] = Load(b@[[storage]], offset = -8, ControlDependent|Reads:Butterfly_publicLength)
# CHECK-NEXT: Int64 b@[[wide]] = ZExt32(b@[[length]])
# CHECK: Int32 b@[[isShort]] = BelowEqual(b@[[wide]], $16(b@{{*}}))
# CHECK-NEXT: Branch(b@[[isShort]], Terminal)
# CHECK-NEXT: Successors: Then:#{{*}}, Else:Rare:#
# CHECK-LABEL: end of function
# A turn of the search among integers: one load of the boxed element, one comparison with the boxed value, the counter, its test. Nothing is unboxed, called or loaded again.
# LOOP-LABEL: loop #
# LOOP-NEXT: BB#
# LOOP: Int64 b@[[element]] = Load(b@{{*}}, ControlDependent|Reads:indexedInt32Properties)
# LOOP-NEXT: Int32 b@[[isFound]] = Equal(b@{{*}}, b@[[element]])
# LOOP-NEXT: Branch(b@[[isFound]], Terminal)
# LOOP-NOT: Reads:
# LOOP-NOT: Patchpoint(
# LOOP-LABEL: end of loop
# The search among doubles compares doubles.
# LOOP-LABEL: loop #
# LOOP: Double b@[[number]] = Load(b@{{*}}, ControlDependent|Reads:indexedDoubleProperties)
# LOOP-NEXT: Int32 b@[[isSame]] = Equal(b@{{*}}, b@[[number]])
# LOOP-NEXT: Branch(b@[[isSame]], Terminal)
# LOOP-NOT: Reads:
# LOOP-NOT: Patchpoint(
# LOOP-LABEL: end of loop
# X64: loop #{{*}}, instructions: 3, patchpoints: 0
# ARM64: loop #{{*}}, instructions: 4, patchpoints: 0
# Only a list in another kind of storage calls Array.prototype.indexOf itself, the one call that can throw. Nothing reads the member by name or tests which function it holds.
# CALLS-LABEL: name="find" role=Source
# CALLS-NOT: :PropGet
# CALLS-NOT: ExitsSideways
# CALLS: ExitsSideways{{*}}:CallBuiltin)
# CALLS-NOT: ExitsSideways
# CALLS-NOT: :PropGet
# CALLS-LABEL: end of function
# The counts of the whole function hold calls, whose moves follow the calling convention: not for Windows.
# X64SIZE: instructions: 46, patchpoints: 2, rare instructions: 14
# ARM64SIZE: instructions: 43, patchpoints: 2, rare instructions: 14
